<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kirkwall</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kirkwall is the main town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a>, on the island of Mainland in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>. It grew around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-magnus-cathedral">St Magnus Cathedral</a>, begun in 1137, and became the seat of the earls and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Orkney, whose palaces stand beside the cathedral. It was made a royal burgh in 1486 after the islands passed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> to Scotland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kirkwall.jpg" alt="Kirkwall" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stevekeiretsu · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kirkwall_Harbour.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
